                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[b]Please consider, that I follow this game since its first demo, I got it before the steam release so I have much more time in it than my profile suggests.[/b]\n\n[h1]Short review[/h1]\n[b]I strongly recommend[/b] the game for those who enjoy story oriented/logic/horror games. The game is challenging and has a nice art style.\n\n[h1]Longer review[/h1]\nAs the description says you will have to collect stuff and create equipment to challenge your enemies, but more importantly the story will be able to keep you in front of your PC until the end. \nThe game has a very nice and polished art style. It has its [b]very own atmosphere[/b], the world is living and disturbing. Sounds are okay as well.\nThe overall game experience is polished and smooth, the game is stable and has a [b]lot of content[/b] in it. \n\nUnfortunately, the trailer is weak in my opinion, you don't really get a good picture of the game. Basically, it's just a short gameplay video. What a pity!\n\nWhat I didn't like is the jumping/running part. It's a bit hard, but still, not overwhelming, you will get over it. Also, maybe it's conceptional, but I missed music. The game has some, but it builds on noise and other sounds, but not really on music.\n\nWe really need original indie games here on Steam. [b]Don't wait, support[/b]!",
                        "timestamp_created": 1500683899,
